From a63105eefc15e4959f4ac667c5542a3359607000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 16:34:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 091/258] feat(pypto-x): ingest qwen35 bf16 checkpoint into
 binding contract

Add a dependency-free safetensors reader plus a programmatic mapping from the
frozen Qwen3.5-0.8B text decoder contract to the official checkpoint tensors,
and emit an auditable storage-relative packed layout for the 320 parameters.

- safetensors_reader: 8-byte length + JSON header, 13 dtypes, strict
  contiguity/no-overlap/coverage validation, read-only mmap or pread views,
  streaming sha256; never materializes the data section.
- qwen35_weight_map: expands the 22 compact manifest storage classes into
  official HuggingFace names, checks contract/manifest/checkpoint three-way
  agreement, records the tie_word_embeddings fallback to embed_tokens, and
  lists the vision tower (153 tensors) and MTP (15 tensors) exclusions with
  counts and bytes.
- qwen35_weight_layout: merges the frozen 368-region packed layout with real
  checkpoint file offsets, verifies the align_up chain, and quantifies the one
  real contract difference: 36 F32 tensors (A_log, linear_attn.norm.weight)
  against the all-bf16 contract. Conversion uses IEEE-754 RNE, not truncation;
  measured A_log round-trip is exact and norm.weight stays within 2^-8.
- tests: synthetic safetensors fixtures with negative cases, 320/320 mapping,
  byte decomposition, layout reproducibility and the real checkpoint (skipped
  when the pinned revision asset is absent).
- python/pypto/portable/__init__.py: the only pre-existing file touched; it
  only re-exports the new public symbols.
